= The Second Askew cabinet

The constant pressure from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span>, along with the scheming of DuFour and his inner circle, has finally forced Askew to reorganize his cabinet to the right. However, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span> remains excluded, as they remain uncompromising in their opposition to Askew.

This move may temporarily soothe DuFour’s displeasure, but it leaves Askew’s position substantially weakened and increasingly dependent on the whims of the presidential palace.

We must now decide whether to continue tolerating this more right-leaning Askew government—now absent of leftist figures such as the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]’s Joseph Werth—or to finally use this as a pretext to break away from it, as Askew has introduced his third emergency decree, which further reduces salaries, and cuts pensions and welfare benefits to address the deficit caused by the banking crisis.

- @vote_yes
- @vote_no

@vote_no
title: Vote against the Second Askew cabinet, ending the toleration agreement.
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; second_bruning_cabinet_dead = 1
call: set_next_election_time

We have officially broken with the [+ chancellor +] government, voting against them in a vote of no confidence. Continuing to support such a government would go against all our values. The propertied parties have also joined in, choosing to cut their losses rather than engage in a futile attempt to save Askew’s government.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year + 2365 +].

@vote_yes
title: Vote in favor of this measure to continue the toleration agreement.
view-if: marcher_toleration
on-arrival: left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 5; commons_marcher -= 3; commons_royalist += 2; commons_collectivist += 1; disfavored_marcher -= 3; disfavored_royalist += 2; disfavored_collectivist += 1; collectivist_relation -= 5

We are compelled once again to vote in favor of the [+ chancellor +] government to prevent the extremist parties on the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">left</span> from translating their growing popular support into parliamentary gains.

Despite the new right-wing cabinet, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span> is still refusing to support Askew, as they want all the power to themselves. 